        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ui): bound Nostr profile write/read requests",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `putNostrProfile` and `importNostrProfile` helpers in `ui/src/pages/channels/nostr-profile-ops.ts` issue `fetch` requests to the gateway/relay Nostr profile endpoint **without any timeout or abort signal**. A stalled or unreachable endpoint hangs the channels page indefinitely while it awaits the response.\n\nThis mirrors the same class of unbounded-network-operation fixes (e.g. `fix(ci)`, `fix(docker)`, `fix(doctor)` \"bound X\" PRs): an unterminated request with no `AbortSignal` can block the UI forever.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdd an `AbortController` + `setTimeout` watchdog (`NOSTR_PROFILE_FETCH_TIMEOUT_MS = 15_000`) to both fetches, following the existing Control UI convention used by `browser-client.ts`, `custom-theme.ts`, and `agent-select.ts`. The timeout is cleared in `finally` so no timer leaks.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThe channels Nostr profile publish/import actions now fail fast instead of hanging when the relay is slow or down.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `ui/src/pages/channels/nostr-profile-ops.ts` on `main`: both `fetch` calls have no `signal`.\n- Fix threads `controller.signal` into both requests and clears the timeout in `finally`.\n- Added `ui/src/pages/channels/nostr-profile-ops.test.ts` exercising the real fetch path against a local HTTP server (not a fetch mock): stalled responses abort after the bound; normal 200 responses still resolve.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nBehavior or issue addressed: Nostr profile publish/import (`putNostrProfile`, `importNostrProfile`) hang the channels page forever when the gateway/relay endpoint never responds, because the fetch has no abort signal.\n\nReal environment tested: macOS 15, Node v24.18.0 (Homebrew node@24), vitest 4.1.9, local HTTP server (`node:http`) bound to 127.0.0.1:0. Real `fetch` is used against that server; only relative-URL resolution is bridged to the local origin.\n\nExact steps or command run after this patch:\n- `npx vitest run ui/src/pages/channels/nostr-profile-ops.test.ts`\n- The stall cases use `vi.useFakeTimers()` + `vi.advanceTimersByTimeAsync(15_000)` to fire the AbortController watchdog without waiting in real time, then assert the call rejects.\n\nEvidence after fix:\n```\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  4 passed (4)\n - aborts a stalled putNostrProfile after the bound instead of hanging  (pass)\n - aborts a stalled importNostrProfile after the bound instead of hanging (pass)\n - still resolves a normal putNostrProfile round trip                  (pass)\n - still resolves a normal importNostrProfile round trip                (pass)\n```\n\nObserved result after fix: With the server accepting the connection but never ending the response, both helpers reject (AbortError) after the 15s bound instead of remaining pending. With the server returning 200 JSON, both helpers resolve and return `{ ok: true, persisted: true }`, so ordinary profile operations are unaffected.\n\nWhat was not tested: A full live Control UI browser session against a real Nostr relay was not executed (no relay credentials / headless browser in this environment). The proof exercises the exact production fetch/timeout/abort code path against a real local server, which is the behavior the change governs; the browser-only difference is relative-URL resolution, which is bridged in the test.\n",
        "branch": "fix/ui-nostr-profile-fetch-timeout",
